---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About">
  <article class="wrap about">
    <img class="mark" src="/avatar.png" alt="A snake biting its own tail, lettered CALCULEMUS on one side and CALCVL·M·S on the other." width="200" height="200" />

    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Let Us Calculate</h1>

      <p>
        Three centuries ago, Leibniz dreamed of a universal symbolic language: when philosophers disagree, they
        would no longer argue, they would simply sit down and say to each other: <i>calculemus</i>, let us calculate. Today’s AI looks like a half-finished
        version of that dream. Machines have started to calculate with language.
      </p>

      <p>This channel explores philosophy, cognitive science and linguistics in an age of AI:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>What does it mean for a language model to “understand” a sentence?</li>
        <li>Can meaning be learned from text alone?</li>
        <li>How do small words like “might” and “must” shape reasoning, in humans and in models?</li>
        <li>What happens when machines increasingly read what machines wrote?</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where to watch</h2>
      <p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/@letuscalculate">YouTube · @letuscalculate</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 8vh, 4.5rem);
  }

  .mark {
    display: block;
    width: 160px;
    height: auto;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem -12px;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.1rem);
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.1em;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.35em;
  }

  li::marker {
    color: var(--red);
  }
</style>
